# flatbuffers is a third-party header-only library, vendored for the capture
# tooling. It is not this project's code and should not count as its language.
mesa/flatbuffers/** linguist-vendored

# Kernel and mesa changes live here as patches, which Linguist reads as Diff
# and does not count. That is why the tracked source is mostly the Python
# analysis and model-building tooling, and why the repository reports Python:
# the driver's C is either in patches or in the gitignored mesa checkout.
*.patch linguist-language=Diff
